h 16 Noes it is not near-unanimous. The vote happened during his current term.\n- **Why rung 2:** Section 220.5 of the bill says schools \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require\" staff to disclose a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. Every clause of rung 2 is in that text.\n- **Why not rung 1:** Section 220.3 only says staff \"shall not be required to disclose\". It does not order staff to keep the information from parents, so rung 1 is ruled out.\n- **What the chair rests on:** it is one record, made of two pages: the vote page and the bill text. Under the codebook that counts as a single source.\n- **Left empty:** there are no quotes, because neither page has Fong's own words. Nothing is listed as a missing source.\n\nSeparately, the session reported that several connected services need authorization in your claude.ai connector settings: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey and WorkOS. The GitHub plugin also failed to connect. None of them were needed for this task.","ttft_ms":8217,"type":"result","duration_ms":25552,"uuid":"895c52b6-1026-466b-90b4-6d2b6f58dad3","ttft_stream_ms":2131,"time_to_request_ms":228,"first_content_frame_ms":2131,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
